    "lawCode": "Add §1393, RPAP L",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Actions and Proceedings Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S3933\n\nSPONSOR: KENNEDY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the real property actions and proceedings law, in\nrelation to prohibiting the registration of mortgages in default prior\nto the filing of a notice of pendency\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to protect mortgagors in distress from\nunreasonable fines and other conditions associated with mortgage fore-\nclosure registries.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 adds a new section 1393 to the real property actions and\nproceedings law to prohibit municipalities from creating a registry of\nresidential mortgages in default prior to a mortgagee filing a notice of\npendency in a court of competent jurisdiction, and to put in place\nsensible rules, including prohibiting the passing along of fines to a\nmortgagor in default when such a registry is created.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAcross the state, mortgage in default registries are rising in populari-\nty. Municipalities often contract with a third party to administer such\nregistries, and they often have hefty and unreasonable fees or other\nconditions attached, which may ultimately be passed on to the mortgagor.\n\nThis legislation is necessary to implement sensible restrictions and\nparameters for municipalities considering such a registry.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2020: S.8915 Referred to Rules I A.10898 Referred to Judiciary\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nMinimal.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
